    > 10.0 => "Too high",
    double.NaN => "Unknown",
    _ => "Acceptable",
};
```

In a relational pattern, use any of the [relational operators](comparison-operators) `<`, `>`, `<=`, or `>=`. The right-hand part of a relational pattern must be a constant expression. The constant expression can be of an [integer](../builtin-types/integral-numeric-types), [floating-point](../builtin-types/floating-point-numeric-types), [char](../builtin-types/char), or [enum](../builtin-t

